  "aiContextParagraph": "The United States has proposed a 25% tariff on goods from India, linking the move to a Section 301 investigation regarding manufacturing capacity. US authorities have expressed concerns that certain national policies contribute to excess capacity, an issue that also impacts major trading partners like China and the European Union. In response, the Indian government has initiated an examination of the US notice, categorically rejecting claims that any domestic sectors are experiencing surplus manufacturing capacity. These trade tensions emerge alongside broader discussions regarding technology supply chains and US regulations on high-end hardware, such as Nvidia artificial intelligence chips. As both nations move toward upcoming trade talks, officials in India have emphasized the need to resolve these tariff concerns through dialogue, while domestic media outlets continue to monitor the potential impact on economic initiatives like Atmanirbhar Bharat.",
